<title>JAPAN: Japan April crude steel output up 7.8 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan April crude steel output up 7.8 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's crude steel output rose 7.8 percent in April from a year earlier to 8.83 million tonnes, the Japan Iron and Steel Federation said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>The April figure was down 0.8 percent from March, the industry group said in a statement.</p>
<p>April output of tin plate was 117,800 tonnes, down 0.9 percent year-on-year and down 8.5 percent month-on-month, the federation said.</p>
<p>Production of galvanised steel sheet in April was 1.02 million tonnes, up 6.9 percent year-on-year and down 11.0 percent month-on-month, it said.</p>
</text>
